  <h1>Press</h1>
  <p class="entrada"><em>Sin motivo</em>: a sky on the web where every blockchain gift becomes a permanent asterisk. Today it is empty.</p>

  <p>A net art work by Solzimer, ongoing since 29 October 2026. It is not a donation: it funds nothing and promises nothing. It is a question: <strong>does anyone give something just because?</strong></p>

  <p class="dato">Texts current as of 12 November 2026. They may be copied as is. <em>Sin motivo</em> is Spanish for “for no reason”; the title is not translated.</p>

  <h2>Short text</h2>
  <p><em>Sin motivo</em> (“for no reason”) is a net art work by Solzimer, ongoing since 29 October 2026. It is a sky. Every gift sent on-chain to the work's address becomes a permanent asterisk. It is not a donation: it funds nothing and promises nothing. It is a question: does anyone give something just because? Today the sky is empty.</p>

  <h2>Medium text</h2>
  <p><em>Sin motivo</em> (“for no reason”) is a participatory net art work by Solzimer, ongoing since 29 October 2026 at salehoy.com.ar. It is a sky. Every gift of ETH or USDC sent on the Base network to the work's address becomes a permanent asterisk, from the Greek <em>asteriskos</em>, “little star”. Each asterisk takes its shape from the transaction's identifier, never from the amount. The amount and the giver are not shown: every gift is worth the same. Visits, by contrast, leave trails that fade.</p>
  <p>The sky turns once per sidereal day. Gifts made on the same day form constellations. The work shows how long it has been since anyone gave.</p>
  <p>It is not a donation and not a sale: it funds nothing, promises nothing and gives nothing in return. It is a question: does anyone give something just because? As of 12 November 2026 there are no gifts. The sky is empty, and that too is part of the work.</p>
  <p class="dato">The long text, the FAQ and the full fact sheet are in the <a href="/prensa/sin-motivo-press-en.md">press kit</a>.</p>

  <h2>Quick facts</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Title:</strong> <em>Sin motivo</em>.</li>
    <li><strong>Artist:</strong> Solzimer (pseudonym).</li>
    <li><strong>Year:</strong> 2026–ongoing. Started on 29 October 2026.</li>
    <li><strong>Type:</strong> net art, participatory work.</li>
    <li><strong>Medium:</strong> website and blockchain ({RED.nombre}, chain {RED.chainId}).</li>
    <li><strong>Gifts that count:</strong> native ETH and official USDC on Base.</li>
    <li><strong>Gifts received as of 12 November 2026:</strong> none.</li>
    <li><strong>Shape of each asterisk:</strong> derived from the transaction's identifier, never from the amount.</li>
    <li><strong>What is not shown:</strong> the amount and the giver.</li>
    <li><strong>Dedication:</strong> optional, ETH only, up to 80 characters, written in the transaction.</li>
    <li><strong>The sky:</strong> a real-time scene that responds to touch, to the mouse and to the tilt of a phone. It turns once per sidereal day.</li>
    <li><strong>Sound:</strong> generated sound layer, optional. It never starts on its own.</li>
    <li><strong>Trails:</strong> visitors can save their own as an image or a video and share it with a link of its own.</li>
    <li><strong>Record:</strong> the server verifies every gift directly against the Base network, with no keys and no paid services. The state of the sky is published at <a href="/api/cielo">/api/cielo</a>, a read-only API.</li>
    <li><strong>Privacy:</strong> uses Google Analytics (with cookies) to count visits; does not ask for or store names, emails or wallet addresses.</li>
    <li><strong>Technique:</strong> JavaScript with no UI framework, static site built with Astro, Netlify.</li>
    <li><strong>Languages:</strong> Spanish, English, Portuguese, French, Italian, German, Chinese, Japanese.</li>
  </ul>
